# Churn Prediction Backend

Spring Boot + Weka (Random Forest) service for real-time customer churn prediction.

## Stack
- Java 17, Spring Boot 3.2
- Weka 3.8.6 (`weka-stable`) — Random Forest classifier
- MySQL 8 (Spring Data JPA / Hibernate)
- Maven

## 1. Prerequisites
- JDK 17+
- Maven 3.8+
- MySQL 8 running locally (or update `application.properties`)

## 2. Database setup
```sql
CREATE DATABASE churn_db;
```
The app will auto-create/update the `customers` table on startup (`ddl-auto=update`).
Edit `src/main/resources/application.properties` if your MySQL user/password differ from `root`/`root`.

## 3. Run it
```bash
mvn spring-boot:run
```

On first startup with an empty `customers` table, the app will:
1. Generate ~800 synthetic, behaviorally-correlated customer records (see `SyntheticDataGenerator`)
2. Save them to MySQL
3. Train a Random Forest model (150 trees, 10-fold cross-validated)
4. Persist the trained model to `churn-rf-model.model` in the project root

Subsequent restarts reuse the saved model and existing data.

## 4. API Endpoints

| Method | Path | Description |
|---|---|---|
| GET | `/api/customers?riskLevel=High&segment=Standard&page=0&size=25` | Paginated, filterable customer list |
| GET | `/api/customers/{customerCode}` | Single customer |
| POST | `/api/customers` | Create a customer record |
| POST | `/api/predict` | Run churn prediction on submitted data |
| POST | `/api/model/train` | Retrain on all labeled records in MySQL |
| GET | `/api/model/status` | Model readiness + last evaluation metrics |
| GET | `/api/analytics/summary` | Aggregates for the dashboard (risk distribution, segments, model metrics) |

### Example: predict
```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:8080/api/predict \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "customerCode": "CUST-000123",
    "tenureMonths": 4,
    "monthlyCharges": 89.50,
    "contractType": "Month-to-month",
    "paymentMethod": "Electronic check",
    "internetService": "Fiber optic",
    "techSupport": "No",
    "numSupportCalls": 3,
    "avgMonthlyUsageGb": 62,
    "paperlessBilling": "Yes",
    "multipleLines": "No"
  }'
```
Response:
```json
{
  "customerCode": "CUST-000123",
  "churnProbability": 0.7231,
  "riskLevel": "High",
  "recommendedAction": "Escalate to retention team within 48 hours; consider loyalty offer."
}
```

## 5. Feature engineering
`FeatureEngineeringService` is the single source of truth for the feature schema, shared by
training and inference so they never drift apart. It cleans nulls, derives `avgRevenuePerMonth`
and `supportCallRate`, and encodes categorical fields as Weka nominal attributes.

## 6. Retraining with real data
Replace the synthetic seeding step by loading your own historical, labeled records via
`POST /api/customers` (include `"churned": "Yes"` or `"No"`), then call `POST /api/model/train`.
